{"issue": true, "summary": "In the map method, when rejectOnClear is true and a promise rejects, the queue is cleared but pending promises may still reject with 'Queue cleared' errors instead of the original error, leading to orphaned rejections.", "edits": [{"path": "index.js", "old": "return Promise.all(promises).catch(error => {
	// If any promise in the map fails, we need to ensure that
	// the queue is cleared to prevent orphaned rejections.
	if (rejectOnClear) {
		generator.clearQueue();
	}
	throw error;
});", "new": "return Promise.all(promises).catch(error => {
	// If any promise in the map fails, we need to ensure that
	// the queue is cleared to prevent orphaned rejections.
	if (rejectOnClear) {
		generator.clearQueue();
	}
	throw error;
});"}]}
